From 280047876a827b7d4abddb80f85995f0c1049687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chrisohearn <137103567+chrisohearn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:04:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Engine: the firmware rebuild path picks the row for this
 device

action_rebuild_vendorfw found the install's firmware row by version alone,
taking the first row for the installed macOS version. 27.2 has two
device-restricted rows (26B123 for j714sap, 26B8125 for k114sap), so a K114s
would have rebuilt from the J714s's 26B123. The match now also requires the
row's devices to name this Mac's device class (rows with no device list still
match); it lives in omarchy_firmware.installed_ipsw, beside the filtering
choose_ipsw already uses, so it can be tested without the installer's
interactive main.py.

- Engine: omarchy_firmware.installed_ipsw; the main.py patch calls it in
  place of the version-only loop.
- Engine tests: a K114s gets the 26B8125 row (26.2.125.8.0,0), a J714s the
  26B123 row (26.2.123.0.0,0), an unrestricted row still matches, a foreign
  board gets none, and the patch uses the helper in the rebuild path.
- Engine v0.9.2-omarchy.20261115.d33f2cef00c4, renamed with engine_pin.py
  and repacked from the authenticated engine.28 base: 17914686 bytes, sha256
  eac6cf71489f993e7b24780a5854f41d15b7dab239db3a1b3064d37fa8adc89b, four
  identical repacks.

J714s: the J714s row is first among the 27.2 rows, so a J714s picks the same
row as before; the test asserts it.

Checked: test/all (engine overlay 449, 446 before; engine tooling, scripts,
Packaging), engine_pin.py check, prepare-engine.py. Not run: no installer or
image was built from this, nothing was run on a K114s or a J714s, and the
rebuild-firmware action itself (it needs a Mac) was not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
